	(text_box "4K Direct Carrier V7 - schematic V3 (Claude, 24 Nov 2026). The carrier holds an Opal Kelly XEM8305 and drives the whole 4K head directly: two DF40C-80DP plugs (J5/J6) mate the passive Option B router V3, which carries four ASIC boards (8 ASICs). Sheets: XEM_Power_USB = Carrier V6 (XEM sockets, 12 V input, TPS54429E 3.3 V buck, XEM_PG-gated TLV75515 1.5 V now on VCCO_64/84/85/86, FT232H USB-JTAG) minus the old LDO-board plugs; ASIC_Rails = FPGA-LDO A V24 regulator block (LT3582-12, LT3042/LT3094 +/-8.06 V, 3x LT3042 + 4x TPS7A2015 in SOT-23-5) fed from the carrier +3V3; Router_Interface = J5/J6, rail/AGND/GND ties, NT1, 17 x 1 uF, 17 safe-idle pulls, H5/H6. Sheets connect by global labels (121 signals, 9 rails) and power symbols (+12V, +3V3, +1V5, GND, AGND). Contract: inputs/PIN_MAP_B_V2.csv, inputs/XEM8305_PIN_TABLE_V3.csv, inputs/SYNTHESIS.md sections 3 and 6. Record: BUILD_NOTES.md. Review fixes of 24 Nov 2026 (XEM_PG-gated ASIC enable U21 with D13/R34/C68, C42 DNP, stock swaps U1/U8/FB2, I3 netlist check) are listed in BUILD_NOTES.md, section Verification and fixes; the schematic V2 part swaps (U13-U15/U17 TPS7A2015PDQNR X2SON -> TPS7A2015PDBVR SOT-23-5, L1 3.3 uH XAL5030-332MEC -> 2.2 uH XAL5030-222MEC) in section Schematic V2 part swaps. Schematic V3 (24 Nov 2026, Howard: \"Yes, pin table V3\"): the MC1/MC2 signal labels follow pin table V3, which re-derives the XEM side (net to MC1/MC2 pin and FPGA ball) from the board geometry; the router contract PIN_MAP_B_V2, every net and XDC port name and all parts are unchanged (BUILD_NOTES.md, section Pin table V3). Schematic V9 (26 Nov 2026, Howard: \"Yes, swap D1\"): the 12 V input diode D1 is now the one-direction SMBJ15A (JLC C83846) with its cathode on +12V, in place of the bidirectional SMBJ15CA-13-F, so a reversed 12 V adapter is clamped (sheet XEM_Power_USB, 12 V input box). The matching board is layout V9 (26 Nov 2026, routed, 8 layers; D1 turned 180 degrees on its Carrier V6 pads, copper unchanged): the router plugs J5/J6 are on the bottom at the Carrier V6 LDO plug site (west edge, on a tongue 20.8 mm long) and the regulators sit on and beside the tongue, next to the plugs. On the board the sixteen rail capacitors C51-C55, C57-C67 and the AGND-GND tie NT1 sit at the rail entry between the plugs and the rail test pads, and R19 sits beside TP14; the circuit is unchanged. Not fabrication-ready."
